KG42.register("edges-3e9b86c541837d210f0fa8f5",{"id":"S-3e6453b100370e96","source":"COMP-ebacec241379c91d","type":"links","target":"COMP-851574b724899235","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["18-dlmp_analysis"],"assertions":[{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011::E::v141-c-R011-E001","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","rule_id":"v141-c-R011","rule_ref":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-ebacec241379c91d","target":"COMP-851574b724899235","source_occurrence_id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011::V::clearing.social_welfare","target_occurrence_id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011::V::pricing.local","source_unit_id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-a-M03::clearing.social_welfare","target_unit_id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-a-M03::pricing.local","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Nodal real-power pricing in the SOCP formulation (II). | Proposition 3 marginal-loss derivation for the radial distribution welfare optimization problem. | Real-power DLMP restriction from KKT conditions (45), (55) and (56) of formulation (II).","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g03-E04"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"283911824b8497461ae82f44a097b23bc26468b7dd2fc10397e8d66804e5e1f0","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","source_definition":"Both formulations maximize consumer benefit net of generation cost, with consumption benefits summed over nonroot nodes and generation costs summed over all nodes. Scope: Radial-distribution-network welfare formulations (I) and (II). Welfare maximization is subject to complex-power flow limits in both directions of each line, real and reactive generation and consumption capacity limits, voltage bounds, and real and reactive power balance. Scope: Feasible allocations in the implicit-function welfare formulation (I). The relaxation imposes complex-power flow limits in both line directions, branch voltage-drop equations, conic constraints, nodal real and reactive power balance, voltage bounds including the root, and generation and consumption capacity constraints (4)-(11). Scope: Feasible allocations in the SOCP welfare formulation (II). Line-current magnitude limits may be included analogously to the line-flow constraints, but are omitted from the presented models. Scope: Optional feasibility restrictions in welfare formulations (I) and (II). The second-order cone constraint (20) must hold as an equality. Scope: Physical interpretation of solutions of SOCP welfare formulation (II). Condition: When a solution of the relaxation is to admit a physical power-flow interpretation.","target_definition":"Differentiating the generation-cost-minus-consumption-benefit form of the welfare objective with respect to D_n yields the real-power DLMP at location n. Scope: Proposition 3 marginal-loss derivation for the radial distribution welfare optimization problem. Condition: A single marginal resource at bus m is re-dispatched to optimally balance a marginal change dD_n in net power injection at location n. The real-power DLMP at each node equals the multiplier of that node's real-power balance constraint in model (II). Scope: Nodal real-power pricing in the SOCP formulation (II). The DLMP at that location equals the marginal cost of the local resource. Scope: Real-power DLMP restriction from KKT conditions (45), (55) and (56) of formulation (II). Condition: A generator at location i produces strictly within its technical region.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Differentiating the generation-cost-minus-consumption-benefit form of the welfare objective with respect to D_n yields the real-power DLMP at location n. Scope: Proposition 3 marginal-loss derivation for the radial distribution welfare optimization problem. Condition: A single marginal resource at bus m is re-dispatched to optimally balance a marginal change dD_n in net power injection at location n.","expression":"\\lambda_n = \\lambda_m \\left(1 + \\sum_{i\\in E} \\frac{dLosses_i}{dD_n}\\right), \\quad Losses_i = R_i l_i","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x-l-i"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-theta-R-i"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E011","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p03-c1r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II.A Implicit Function Formulation","anchor_text":"y p , de linear functions of voltage magnitude at the root, and net of power injections at all buses","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The objective of (I) is to maximize social welfare. $(I): \\max \\sum_{i\\in N^+} C_i^c p_i^c - \\sum_{i\\in N} C_i^g p_i^g \\quad (1)$"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e14","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C DLMP Decomposition Based on Marginal Losses","anchor_text":"8) C. DLMP Decomposition Based on Marginal Losses 9) An alternative approach towards understanding D","equation_id":"(67)-(68)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In the subsequent proposition we use the following notation for real power losses on a given line i\\in E:\nLosses_i = R_i l_i. \\quad (67)\nProposition 3: Suppose that a single marginal resource is re-dispatched in order to optimally balance a marginal change dD_n in net power injection in location n, and denote m as the bus of the marginal resource. Then the DLMP can be expressed as\n\\lambda_n = \\lambda_m \\left(1 + \\sum_{i\\in E} \\frac{dLosses_i}{dD_n}\\right). \\quad (68)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e15","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p06-c2r3__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"III.C DLMP Decomposition Based on Marginal Losses","anchor_text":"n a i∈E n- Proof: Assume that the marginal resource which is re- nd dispatched is a generator (the p","equation_id":"(69)-(71)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Proof: Assume that the marginal resource which is re-dispatched is a generator (the proof follows analogously if the marginal resource is a consumer). Consider the global power balance equation:\np_m^g = \\sum_{i\\in N^+} p_i^c + \\sum_{i\\in E} Losses_i - \\sum_{i\\in N-\\{m\\}} p_i^g, \\quad (69)\nwhere m is the marginal generator. Substituting into the objective function,\n\\sum_{i\\in N} C_i^g p_i^g - \\sum_{i\\in N^+} C_i^c p_i^c = \\sum_{i\\in N-\\{m\\}} C_i^g p_i^g - \\sum_{i\\in N^+} C_i^c p_i^c\n+ C_m^g \\left(\\sum_{i\\in N^+} p_i^c + \\sum_{i\\in E} Losses_i - \\sum_{i\\in N-\\{m\\}} p_i^g\\right). \\quad (70)\nDifferentiating the objective function with respect to D_n yields the DLMP at location n. On the other hand, we have that \\lambda_m = C_m^g. Moreover, by definition of the marginal resource, the derivative of p_i^g with respect to D_n is equal to zero for all i\\neq m and the derivative of p_i^c with respect to D_n is also zero for all i\\in N^+. We thus arrive to the following identity:\n\\lambda_n = \\lambda_m \\left(1 + \\sum_{i\\in E} \\frac{dLosses_i}{dD_n}\\right). \\quad (71)"}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Nodal real-power pricing in the SOCP formulation (II). | Proposition 3 marginal-loss derivation for the radial distribution welfare optimization problem. | Real-power DLMP restriction from KKT conditions (45), (55) and (56) of formulation (II).","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-e12","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15","v141-b-g03-E04"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E011","v141-b-g02-e14","v141-b-g02-e15"]},"paper_scope_note":"The common transmission-distribution coordination framework, the reviewed aggregator market, and the radial model of this paper are kept separate; the DLMP multiple-solution risk is retained, and network feasibility cannot be asserted from the price signal."}}],"assertion_ids":["18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R011::E::v141-c-R011-E001"]});
